  "title": "Fix a few proto_tree_add_uint_format calls with length -1",
  "description": "A length -1 for a FT_UINT doesn't work, and hasn't worked at least since\nbefore Wireshark 1.8, possibly longer. Some of these might have been\ntext-only nodes. These are generally some kind of information stored\nfrom a request being echoed in the reply. It makes more sense to have\nthese be length 0 generated items than span the entire tvbuffer. There\nare already other items (FT_PROTOCOL, FT_BYTES) that do that here.\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
  "state": "merged",
